IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc26-interpretation`

-- ccc26-hearing.l4 -- sections 723 to 729.1 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: submissions and evidence at sentencing, facts, other
-- offences, the offender's chance to speak, reasons and endorsements, previous convictions, the justified sentence, and the analyst's certificate
-- (lines 15377-15466 of the text). Layer 1 of part ccc26. The text is a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation; it is not the official text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- The directions here are addressed to the court; each is encoded for what it decides for the person sentenced.

§ `Section 723 -- Submissions on facts; evidence`

-- src:15377 | Submissions on facts
-- src:15378 | 723 (1) Before determining the sentence, a court shall give the prosecutor and the offender an opportunity to make submissions with respect to any facts relevant to the sentence to be imposed.
@ref s 723(1) (src:15377-15378)
GIVEN `the sentence has not yet been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 723(1) the court must give the prosecutor and the offender an opportunity to make submissions on the facts` MEANS
    IF `the sentence has not yet been determined`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before determining the sentence, a court shall give the prosecutor and the offender an opportunity to make submissions"

-- src:15379 | Submission of evidence
-- src:15380 | (2) The court shall hear any relevant evidence presented by the prosecutor or the offender.
@ref s 723(2) (src:15379-15380)
GIVEN `the evidence is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is presented by the prosecutor or the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 723(2) the court must hear the evidence` MEANS
    IF `the evidence is relevant` AND `the evidence is presented by the prosecutor or the offender`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court shall hear any relevant evidence presented by the prosecutor or the offender"

-- src:15381 | Production of evidence
-- src:15382 | (3) The court may, on its own motion, after hearing argument from the prosecutor and the offender, require the production of evidence that would assist it in determining the appropriate sentence.
@ref s 723(3) (src:15381-15382)
GIVEN `the court acts on its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has heard argument from the prosecutor and the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence would assist the court in determining the appropriate sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 723(3) the court may require the production of the evidence` MEANS   -- gate: on (its own motion), after (hearing argument)
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the court acts on its own motion`) OR (NOT `the court has heard argument from the prosecutor and the offender`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court may, on its own motion, after hearing argument from the prosecutor and the offender"
        IF NOT `the evidence would assist the court in determining the appropriate sentence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "require the production of evidence that would assist it in determining the appropriate sentence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15383 | Compel appearance
-- src:15384 | (4) Where it is necessary in the interests of justice, the court may, after consulting the parties, compel the appearance of any person who is a compellable witness to assist the court in determining the appropriate sentence.
@ref s 723(4) (src:15383-15384)
GIVEN `it is necessary in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has consulted the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a compellable witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appearance is to assist the court in determining the appropriate sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 723(4) the court may compel the appearance of the person` MEANS   -- gate: where (necessary in the interests of justice), after (consulting the parties)
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `it is necessary in the interests of justice`) OR (NOT `the court has consulted the parties`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it is necessary in the interests of justice, the court may, after consulting the parties"
        IF (NOT `the person is a compellable witness`) OR (NOT `the appearance is to assist the court in determining the appropriate sentence`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "compel the appearance of any person who is a compellable witness to assist the court in determining the appropriate sentence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15385 | Hearsay evidence
-- src:15386 | (5) Hearsay evidence is admissible at sentencing proceedings, but the court may, if the court considers it to be in the interests of justice, compel a person to testify where the person
@ref s 723(5) (src:15385-15386)
GIVEN `the evidence is hearsay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are sentencing proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 723(5) hearsay evidence is admissible at the sentencing proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the evidence is hearsay` AND `the proceedings are sentencing proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Hearsay evidence is admissible at sentencing proceedings"

-- src:15385 | Hearsay evidence
-- src:15386 | (5) Hearsay evidence is admissible at sentencing proceedings, but the court may, if the court considers it to be in the interests of justice, compel a person to testify where the person
-- src:15387 | (a) has personal knowledge of the matter;
-- src:15388 | (b) is reasonably available; and
-- src:15389 | (c) is a compellable witness.
@ref s 723(5) (src:15385-15389)
GIVEN `the person has personal knowledge of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is reasonably available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a compellable witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers it to be in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 723(5) the court may compel the person to testify` MEANS   -- gate: where (the person has personal knowledge, is reasonably available and is a compellable witness), if (the court considers it in the interests of justice)
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person has personal knowledge of the matter`) OR (NOT `the person is reasonably available`) OR (NOT `the person is a compellable witness`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "compel a person to testify where the person (a) has personal knowledge of the matter; (b) is reasonably available; and (c) is a compellable witness"
        IF NOT `the court considers it to be in the interests of justice` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the court considers it to be in the interests of justice"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 724 -- Information accepted; facts; disputed facts`

-- src:15390 | Information accepted
-- src:15391 | 724 (1) In determining a sentence, a court may accept as proved any information disclosed at the trial or at the sentencing proceedings and any facts agreed on by the prosecutor and the offender.
@ref s 724(1) (src:15390-15391)
GIVEN `the court is determining a sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was disclosed at the trial or at the sentencing proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facts were agreed on by the prosecutor and the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 724(1) the court may accept the information or facts as proved` MEANS   -- gate: in (determining a sentence)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is determining a sentence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In determining a sentence, a court may accept as proved"
        IF `the information was disclosed at the trial or at the sentencing proceedings` OR `the facts were agreed on by the prosecutor and the offender` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any information disclosed at the trial or at the sentencing proceedings and any facts agreed on by the prosecutor and the offender"

-- src:15392 | Jury
-- src:15393 | (2) Where the court is composed of a judge and jury, the court
-- src:15394 | (a) shall accept as proven all facts, express or implied, that are essential to the jury’s verdict of guilty; and
@ref s 724(2)(a) (src:15392-15394)
GIVEN `the court is composed of a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fact is essential to the jury's verdict of guilty, expressly or by implication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 724(2)(a) the court must accept the fact as proven` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is composed of a judge and jury` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court is composed of a judge and jury, the court (a) shall accept as proven"
        IF NOT `the fact is essential to the jury's verdict of guilty, expressly or by implication` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all facts, express or implied, that are essential to the jury's verdict of guilty"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15395 | (b) may find any other relevant fact that was disclosed by evidence at the trial to be proven, or hear evidence presented by either party with respect to that fact.
@ref s 724(2)(b) (src:15395)
GIVEN `the court is composed of a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fact is another relevant fact that was disclosed by evidence at the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 724(2)(b) the court may find the fact proven or hear evidence on it` MEANS   -- gate: where (the court is composed of a judge and jury)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is composed of a judge and jury` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court is composed of a judge and jury, the court"
        IF NOT `the fact is another relevant fact that was disclosed by evidence at the trial` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other relevant fact that was disclosed by evidence at the trial"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15396 | Disputed facts
-- src:15397 | (3) Where there is a dispute with respect to any fact that is relevant to the determination of a sentence,
-- src:15398 | (a) the court shall request that evidence be adduced as to the existence of the fact unless the court is satisfied that sufficient evidence was adduced at the trial;
@ref s 724(3)(a) (src:15396-15398)
