      `the court is satisfied that sufficient evidence was adduced at the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 724(3)(a) the court must request that evidence be adduced as to the existence of the fact` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `there is a dispute with respect to a fact that is relevant to the determination of a sentence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is a dispute with respect to any fact that is relevant to the determination of a sentence"
        IF `the court is satisfied that sufficient evidence was adduced at the trial` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court is satisfied that sufficient evidence was adduced at the trial"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15399 | (b) the party wishing to rely on a relevant fact, including a fact contained in a presentence report, has the burden of proving it;
@ref s 724(3)(b) (src:15399)
GIVEN `there is a dispute with respect to a fact that is relevant to the determination of a sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party wishes to rely on the fact, including a fact contained in a presentence report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 724(3)(b) the party has the burden of proving the fact` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `there is a dispute with respect to a fact that is relevant to the determination of a sentence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is a dispute with respect to any fact that is relevant to the determination of a sentence"
        IF NOT `the party wishes to rely on the fact, including a fact contained in a presentence report` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the party wishing to rely on a relevant fact, including a fact contained in a presentence report, has the burden of proving it"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15400 | (c) either party may cross-examine any witness called by the other party;
@ref s 724(3)(c) (src:15400)
GIVEN `there is a dispute with respect to a fact that is relevant to the determination of a sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witness was called by the other party` IS A BOOLEAN
