§ `Section 725 -- Other offences`

-- src:15403 | Other offences
-- src:15404 | 725 (1) In determining the sentence, a court
-- src:15405 | (a) shall consider, if it is possible and appropriate to do so, any other offences of which the offender was found guilty by the same court, and shall determine the sentence to be imposed for each of those offences;
@ref s 725(1)(a) (src:15403-15405)
GIVEN `the offender was found guilty of the other offence by the same court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is possible and appropriate to consider it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 725(1)(a) the court must consider the other offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offender was found guilty of the other offence by the same court` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other offences of which the offender was found guilty by the same court"
        IF NOT `it is possible and appropriate to consider it` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is possible and appropriate to do so"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 725(1)(a) (src:15405)
GIVEN `the court considers the other offence under paragraph 725(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 725(1)(a) the court must determine the sentence to be imposed for the other offence` MEANS
    IF `the court considers the other offence under paragraph 725(1)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and shall determine the sentence to be imposed for each of those offences"

-- src:15406 | (b) shall consider, if the Attorney General and the offender consent, any outstanding charges against the offender to which the offender consents to plead guilty and pleads guilty, if the court has jurisdiction to try those charges, and shall determine the sentence to be imposed for each charge unless the court is of the opinion that a separate prosecution for the other offence is necessary in the public interest;
@ref s 725(1)(b) (src:15406)
GIVEN `s 2 Attorney General: the person who consented is the Attorney General` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `that person has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender consents to plead guilty to the outstanding charge and pleads guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has jurisdiction to try the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 725(1)(b) the court must consider the outstanding charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 Attorney General: the person who consented is the Attorney General` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): who is the Attorney General for this proceeding is for section 2
        IF (NOT ((`s 2 Attorney General: the person who consented is the Attorney General` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `that person has consented`)) OR (NOT `the offender consents`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Attorney General and the offender consent"
        IF NOT `the court has jurisdiction to try the charge` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the court has jurisdiction to try those charges"
        IF NOT `the offender consents to plead guilty to the outstanding charge and pleads guilty` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any outstanding charges against the offender to which the offender consents to plead guilty and pleads guilty"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 725(1)(b) (src:15406)
GIVEN `the court considers the charge under paragraph 725(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is of the opinion that a separate prosecution for the other offence is necessary in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 725(1)(b) the court must determine the sentence to be imposed for the charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court considers the charge under paragraph 725(1)(b)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and shall determine the sentence to be imposed for each charge"
        IF `the court is of the opinion that a separate prosecution for the other offence is necessary in the public interest` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court is of the opinion that a separate prosecution for the other offence is necessary in the public interest"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15407 | (b.1) shall consider any outstanding charges against the offender, unless the court is of the opinion that a separate prosecution for one or more of the other offences is necessary in the public interest, subject to the following conditions:
