§ `Section 727 -- Previous conviction`

-- (1): a bar. "Subject to subsections (3) and (4)" displaces it; "unless the prosecutor satisfies the court" lifts it.
-- src:15435 | Previous conviction
-- src:15436 | 727 (1) Subject to subsections (3) and (4), where an offender is convicted of an offence for which a greater punishment may be imposed by reason of previous convictions, no greater punishment shall be imposed on the offender by reason thereof unless the prosecutor satisfies the court that the offender, before making a plea, was notified that a greater punishment would be sought by reason thereof.
@ref s 727(1) (src:15435-15436)
GIVEN `the offender is convicted of an offence for which a greater punishment may be imposed by reason of previous convictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 727(3) or (4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor satisfies the court that the offender, before making a plea, was notified that a greater punishment would be sought by reason of the previous convictions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 727(1) a greater punishment by reason of previous convictions is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offender is convicted of an offence for which a greater punishment may be imposed by reason of previous convictions` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an offender is convicted of an offence for which a greater punishment may be imposed by reason of previous convictions"
        IF `subsection 727(3) or (4) applies` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsections (3) and (4)"
        IF `the prosecutor satisfies the court that the offender, before making a plea, was notified that a greater punishment would be sought by reason of the previous convictions` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the prosecutor satisfies the court that the offender, before making a plea, was notified that a greater punishment would be sought by reason thereof"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15437 | Procedure
-- src:15438 | (2) Where an offender is convicted of an offence for which a greater punishment may be imposed by reason of previous convictions, the court shall, on application by the prosecutor and on being satisfied that the offender was notified in accordance with subsection (1), ask whether the offender was previously convicted and, if the offender does not admit to any previous convictions, evidence of previous convictions may be adduced.
@ref s 727(2) (src:15437-15438)
GIVEN `the offender is convicted of an offence for which a greater punishment may be imposed by reason of previous convictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the offender was notified in accordance with subsection 727(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 727(2) the court must ask whether the offender was previously convicted` MEANS
    IF     `the offender is convicted of an offence for which a greater punishment may be imposed by reason of previous convictions`
       AND `the prosecutor applies`
       AND `the court is satisfied that the offender was notified in accordance with subsection 727(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court shall, on application by the prosecutor and on being satisfied that the offender was notified in accordance with subsection (1), ask whether the offender was previously convicted"

@ref s 727(2) (src:15437-15438)
GIVEN `the court has asked whether the offender was previously convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender does not admit to any previous convictions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 727(2) evidence of previous convictions may be adduced` MEANS   -- gate: if (the offender does not admit to any previous convictions)
    IF `the court has asked whether the offender was previously convicted` AND `the offender does not admit to any previous convictions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the offender does not admit to any previous convictions, evidence of previous convictions may be adduced"

-- src:15439 | Where hearing ex parte
-- src:15440 | (3) Where a summary conviction court holds a trial pursuant to subsection 803(2) and convicts the offender, the court may, whether or not the offender was notified that a greater punishment would be sought by reason of a previous conviction, make inquiries and hear evidence with respect to previous convictions of the offender and, if any such conviction is proved, may impose a greater punishment by reason thereof.
@ref s 727(3) (src:15439-15440)
GIVEN `a summary conviction court holds a trial pursuant to subsection 803(2) and convicts the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 727(3) the court may make inquiries and hear evidence with respect to previous convictions` MEANS   -- gate: where (a summary conviction court holds a trial pursuant to subsection 803(2) and convicts)
    IF `a summary conviction court holds a trial pursuant to subsection 803(2) and convicts the offender`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a summary conviction court holds a trial pursuant to subsection 803(2) and convicts the offender, the court may"

@ref s 727(3) (src:15439-15440)
GIVEN `a summary conviction court holds a trial pursuant to subsection 803(2) and convicts the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a previous conviction is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 727(3) the court may impose a greater punishment by reason of the previous conviction` MEANS   -- gate: where (as above), if (a previous conviction is proved)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a summary conviction court holds a trial pursuant to subsection 803(2) and convicts the offender` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a summary conviction court holds a trial pursuant to subsection 803(2) and convicts the offender, the court may"
        IF NOT `a previous conviction is proved` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if any such conviction is proved, may impose a greater punishment by reason thereof"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15441 | Organizations
-- src:15442 | (4) If, under section 623, the court proceeds with the trial of an organization that has not appeared and pleaded and convicts the organization, the court may, whether or not the organization was notified that a greater punishment would be sought by reason of a previous conviction, make inquiries and hear evidence with respect to previous convictions of the organization and, if any such conviction is proved, may impose a greater punishment by reason of that conviction.
@ref s 727(4) (src:15441-15442)
GIVEN `under section 623 the court proceeds with the trial of an organization that has not appeared and pleaded and convicts the organization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 727(4) the court may make inquiries and hear evidence with respect to previous convictions of the organization` MEANS   -- gate: if (under section 623 the court proceeds with the trial and convicts)
    IF `under section 623 the court proceeds with the trial of an organization that has not appeared and pleaded and convicts the organization`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If, under section 623, the court proceeds with the trial of an organization that has not appeared and pleaded and convicts the organization, the court may"

@ref s 727(4) (src:15441-15442)
GIVEN `under section 623 the court proceeds with the trial of an organization that has not appeared and pleaded and convicts the organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a previous conviction is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 727(4) the court may impose a greater punishment by reason of the previous conviction of the organization` MEANS   -- gate: if (under section 623 the court proceeds with the trial and convicts), if (a previous conviction is proved)
    IF `under section 623 the court proceeds with the trial of an organization that has not appeared and pleaded and convicts the organization` AND `a previous conviction is proved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if any such conviction is proved, may impose a greater punishment by reason of that conviction"

