§ `Section 728 -- Sentence justified by any count`

-- src:15445 | Sentence justified by any count
-- src:15446 | 728 Where one sentence is passed on a verdict of guilty on two or more counts of an indictment, the sentence is good if any of the counts would have justified the sentence.
@ref s 728 (src:15445-15446)
GIVEN `one sentence is passed on a verdict of guilty on two or more counts of an indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any of the counts would have justified the sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 728 makes the sentence good` MEANS
    IF `one sentence is passed on a verdict of guilty on two or more counts of an indictment` AND `any of the counts would have justified the sentence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where one sentence is passed on a verdict of guilty on two or more counts of an indictment, the sentence is good if any of the counts would have justified the sentence"

§ `Sections 729 and 729.1 -- Proof of a certificate of an analyst`

-- src:15447 | Proof of certificate of analyst
-- src:15448 | 729 (1) In
-- src:15449 | (a) a prosecution for failure to comply with a condition in a probation order that the accused not have in possession or use drugs, or
-- src:15450 | (b) a hearing to determine whether the offender breached a condition of a conditional sentence order that the offender not have in possession or use drugs,
-- src:15451 | a certificate purporting to be signed by an analyst stating that the analyst has analyzed or examined a substance and stating the result of the analysis or examination is admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof of the statements contained in the certificate without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate.
@ref s 729(1) (src:15447-15451)
GIVEN `the proceeding is a prosecution for failure to comply with a condition in a probation order that the accused not have in possession or use drugs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is a hearing to determine whether the offender breached a condition of a conditional sentence order that the offender not have in possession or use drugs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 729(2) the signer is an analyst` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the certificate purports to be signed by an analyst, states that the analyst has analyzed or examined a substance and states the result` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 729(1) the certificate is admissible in evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the proceeding is a prosecution for failure to comply with a condition in a probation order that the accused not have in possession or use drugs`) AND (NOT `the proceeding is a hearing to determine whether the offender breached a condition of a conditional sentence order that the offender not have in possession or use drugs`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In (a) a prosecution for failure to comply with a condition in a probation order that the accused not have in possession or use drugs, or (b) a hearing to determine whether the offender breached a condition of a conditional sentence order"
        IF `s 729(2) the signer is an analyst` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the signer is a person designated as an analyst is for the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act and the Cannabis Act
        IF (`s 729(2) the signer is an analyst` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT `the certificate purports to be signed by an analyst, states that the analyst has analyzed or examined a substance and states the result`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a certificate purporting to be signed by an analyst stating that the analyst has analyzed or examined a substance and stating the result of the analysis or examination is admissible in evidence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 729(1) (src:15447-15451)
GIVEN `the certificate is admissible in evidence under subsection 729(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 729(1) the certificate is proof of the statements contained in it, without proof of the signature or official character of the signer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the certificate is admissible in evidence under subsection 729(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof of the statements contained in the certificate"
        IF `the certificate is admissible in evidence under subsection 729(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof of the statements contained in the certificate"

