    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a certificate of an analyst is produced against the party` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The party against whom a certificate of an analyst is produced may"
        IF NOT `the court has given leave` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, with leave of the court, require the attendance of the analyst for cross-examination"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15459 | Proof of certificate of analyst — bodily substance
-- src:15460 | 729.1 (1) In a prosecution for failure to comply with a condition in a probation order that the accused not consume drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance, or in a hearing to determine whether the offender breached such a condition of a conditional sentence order, a certificate purporting to be signed by an analyst that states that the analyst has analyzed a sample of a bodily substance and that states the result of the analysis is admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof of the statements contained in the certificate without proof of the signature or official character of the person who appears to have signed the certificate.
@ref s 729.1(1) (src:15459-15460)
GIVEN `the proceeding is a prosecution for failure to comply with a condition in a probation order that the accused not consume drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance, or a hearing to determine whether the offender breached such a condition of a conditional sentence order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 729.1(2) the signer is an analyst` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the certificate purports to be signed by an analyst, states that the analyst has analyzed a sample of a bodily substance and states the result` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 729.1(1) the certificate is admissible in evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceeding is a prosecution for failure to comply with a condition in a probation order that the accused not consume drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance, or a hearing to determine whether the offender breached such a condition of a conditional sentence order` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In a prosecution for failure to comply with a condition in a probation order that the accused not consume drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance, or in a hearing to determine whether the offender breached such a condition of a conditional sentence order"
        IF `s 729.1(2) the signer is an analyst` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the signer is an analyst is for section 320.11
        IF (`s 729.1(2) the signer is an analyst` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT `the certificate purports to be signed by an analyst, states that the analyst has analyzed a sample of a bodily substance and states the result`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a certificate purporting to be signed by an analyst that states that the analyst has analyzed a sample of a bodily substance and that states the result of the analysis is admissible in evidence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 729.1(1) (src:15459-15460)
GIVEN `the certificate is admissible in evidence under subsection 729.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 729.1(1) the certificate is proof of the statements contained in it, without proof of the signature or official character of the signer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the certificate is admissible in evidence under subsection 729.1(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof of the statements contained in the certificate"
        IF `the certificate is admissible in evidence under subsection 729.1(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof of the statements contained in the certificate"

